  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    Grand Vista Hotel Reservation System is a full-stack Java web application for hotel operations.
    It covers guest management, room management, reservations, payments, staff management, and reviews.
    The system uses JSP for the UI, servlets for controllers, and DAO classes to persist data into text files.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Objectives</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide a complete hotel reservation workflow from browsing to booking and payment.</li>
    <li>Separate guest and staff functionality with role-based access.</li>
    <li>Implement a layered MVC-style architecture using JSP, Servlets, Services, and DAOs.</li>
    <li>Use file-based persistence so the system can run without a database server.</li>
    <li>Support teamwork through git branches and merges.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Technology Stack</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Backend</td><td>Java 11</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Web Framework</td><td>Servlet API 4.0.1, JSP 2.3, JSTL 1.2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Server</td><td>Embedded Apache Tomcat 9.0.109</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Build Tool</td><td>Apache Maven</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>Bootstrap 5, Bootstrap Icons, CSS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Persistence</td><td>Text files under data/</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Version Control</td><td>Git and GitHub</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>4. System Architecture</h2>
  <p>
    The application follows a layered architecture. JSP pages handle presentation, servlets handle routing and
    request logic, services and DAOs handle business rules and file persistence, and model classes represent
    hotel entities.
  </p>
  <p><b>Request Flow:</b> Browser -> JSP/Servlet -> Service/DAO -> Text File -> Response</p>

  <h2>5. Module Details</h2>

  <h3>5.1 Guest Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Registration for Regular or VIP guests, login, profile update, self-delete, and staff-only guest list.</li>
    <li>Email and phone validations are enforced in the registration and update flow.</li>
    <li>Key classes: Guest, RegularGuest, VIPGuest, GuestDAO, GuestServlet.</li>
    <li>Pages: guest/login.jsp, guest/register.jsp, guest/profile.jsp, guest/list.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5.2 Room Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Room listing, search with filters, staff-only add/edit/delete.</li>
    <li>Sorting by price, floor, type, and availability using QuickSort utilities.</li>
    <li>Supports StandardRoom and SuiteRoom with different pricing rules.</li>
    <li>Pages: room/list.jsp, room/search.jsp, room/add.jsp, room/edit.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5.3 Reservation Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Book, modify, view, and cancel reservations. Staff can update reservation status.</li>
    <li>Availability checks are performed for requested date ranges.</li>
    <li>Supports standard, group, and long-stay reservation types.</li>
    <li>Pages: reservation/book.jsp, reservation/modify.jsp, reservation/view.jsp, reservation/list.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5.4 Payment and Billing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Checkout, payment history, and staff-only void/delete operations.</li>
    <li>Guests can pay by credit card; staff can record cash payments.</li>
    <li>Supports payment sorting by date, amount, status, and ID.</li>
    <li>Pages: billing/checkout.jsp, billing/payment.jsp, billing/history.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5.5 Staff Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Staff login and dashboard, manager-only register/edit/delete staff.</li>
    <li>Two staff roles: Manager and Receptionist with different permissions.</li>
    <li>Pages: staff/login.jsp, staff/dashboard.jsp, staff/register.jsp, staff/manage.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5.6 Review Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Guests submit reviews (verified or anonymous). Staff can moderate reviews and respond.</li>
    <li>Reviews are displayed publicly and can be edited.</li>
    <li>Pages: review/view.jsp, review/submit.jsp, review/moderate.jsp.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Object-Oriented Design (OOP)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Abstraction:</b> Guest, Room, Staff, Payment, Review, and AbstractReservation are abstract base classes.</li>
    <li><b>Inheritance:</b> RegularGuest/VIPGuest, StandardRoom/SuiteRoom, Manager/Receptionist, CashPayment/CreditCardPayment, GroupReservation/LongStayReservation.</li>
    <li><b>Polymorphism:</b> calculateDiscount, calculatePrice, processPayment, getReservationType, and calculateCancellationFee are overridden in subclasses.</li>
    <li><b>Encapsulation:</b> Models use private fields with getters/setters.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data Storage</h2>
  <p>Data is stored in text files in the data/ directory:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>data/guests.txt</li>
    <li>data/rooms.txt</li>
    <li>data/reservations.txt</li>
    <li>data/payments.txt</li>
    <li>data/reviews.txt</li>
    <li>data/staff.txt</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Build and Run Instructions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Install Java 11 and Maven.</li>
    <li>Run: mvn clean compile</li>
    <li>Run: mvn exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.hotel.Main"</li>
    <li>Open: http://localhost:8080/</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>9. Testing and Validation (Manual)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Create a guest account and confirm it appears in data/guests.txt.</li>
    <li>Book a reservation and confirm it is listed under reservations.</li>
    <li>Run payment checkout and confirm payment history updates.</li>
    <li>Log in as staff and validate access to management pages.</li>
    <li>Submit a review and confirm it appears in review listing and moderation page.</li>
  </ul>

